 @GregFirehawk  No it isn't. If 8GB is enough for you, then you're not playing anything that requires more than an integrated GPU. Dude, I have an 8GB 7600 and I can run F1 on ultra settings (with RT options off) or Baldur's Gate 3 on max settings and both of those games (which are quite different between each other) have instances where they reach maximum VRAM capacity. 
This means that the card is CAPABLE of running the games, but the performance gets hit by the fact that it lacks VRAM. 

And in the case that you DO need a discrete GPU but not much VRAM (meaning you need frames but you play eSports titles) then in that case you don't need anything new.
